<</A 8685 0 R/Alt(For E[t\(x\)] equals integral from negative infinity to infinity of p\(x\) dot TeLU\(x\) dx equals integral from negative infinity to infinity of 1 over sigma root 2 pi dot exp\(negative x squared over 2 sigma squared\) dot TeLU\(x\) dx to be positive for\
 all sigma in R+, we must show that absolute value of p\(negative epsilon\) TeLU\(negative epsilon\) is less than p\(epsilon\) TeLU\(epsilon\) for all epsilon in R+. In other words, we must show that the positive component of p\(x\) dot TeLU\(x\) is alway\
s a strict upper bound to the absolute value of its negative component, evaluated symmetrically about x equals 0. epsilon equals 0 can be disregarded, as p\(epsilon\) dot TeLU\(epsilon\) equals p\(0\) dot TeLU\(0\) equals 0. Hence, we show that absolute v\
alue of p\(negative epsilon\) dot TeLU\(negative epsilon\) is less than p\(epsilon\) dot TeLU\(epsilon\) for all epsilon in R+.)/C/adbe_style_01c002/ID 8686 0 R/K 69/P 29 0 R/Pg 7298 0 R/S/Figure>>
endobj
